#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Teach delivery leads how to generate context blocks with the `hero "
"relevant` command and incorporate them into engineer instructions before "
"delegating work. Context injection is how agents avoid repeating past "
"mistakes, violating conventions, and contradicting architectural "
"decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Load this skill before the delivery phase of any spec — after the spec is"
" written and before delegating to an engineer or specialist agent. If "
"`hero.json` has `auto_context: true`, the workflow handles this "
"automatically, but delivery leads should still understand the output to "
"intervene when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:17
msgid "What context injection is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Context injection bridges the gap between \"here's what to build\" (the "
"spec) and \"here's what you need to know about this codebase\" (the "
"context). Without it, an agent writes code in isolation — unaware of "
"conventions, past decisions, and known failure modes in the areas it's "
"touching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"The `hero relevant` command queries the spec corpus index and returns a "
"structured block of relevant information. The delivery lead pastes this "
"block into the engineer's instructions alongside the spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:23
msgid "Running hero relevant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:25
msgid "From a spec path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:27
msgid "hero relevant .hero/planning/features/add-csv-export/spec.md\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:31
msgid ""
"This parses the spec's Changes section, extracts file paths mentioned in "
"it, and looks up context for those files. This is the most common usage —"
" you have a spec and want context for the work it describes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:33
msgid "From explicit file paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:35
msgid "hero relevant --files src/api/users.ts src/db/queries/users.sql\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"Use this when you know the files that will be touched but don't have a "
"spec, or when the spec's Changes section doesn't mention specific files "
"yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:41
msgid "Output format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:43
msgid "The command returns a markdown block with up to four sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:45
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"## Context for this work\n"
"\n"
"### Conventions to follow\n"
"- **api-response-format** (scope: src/api/**/*.ts): All API error "
"responses\n"
"  use the ApiError class and return { error, code, details }.\n"
"- **sql-migration-naming** (scope: **/migrations/*.sql): Migration files\n"
"  use the format YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql.\n"
"\n"
"### API surface (when relevant)\n"
"If the spec touches API handler files, run `hero_code endpoints` to get "
"the\n"
"endpoint-to-handler mapping. Include this when work involves routing,\n"
"middleware, or request/response changes so the engineer knows the full\n"
"API surface around the files being modified.\n"
"\n"
"### Past work in this area\n"
"- **add-user-search** (completed): Added full-text search to the users\n"
"  endpoint. Introduced the SearchQuery type in src/api/types.ts.\n"
"\n"
"### Decisions that apply\n"
"- **use-postgres-fts** (accepted): Use PostgreSQL full-text search rather"
"\n"
"  than Elasticsearch for search features under 1M documents.\n"
"\n"
"### Known risks\n"
"- **login-timeout-race** (bug, completed): Race condition in session\n"
"  handling when concurrent requests hit src/api/auth.ts. Fixed by\n"
"  adding mutex on session write.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"Each entry is a summary — enough to inform the agent without overwhelming"
" it. The agent can look up the full spec if it needs more detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:76
msgid "Interpreting the sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:78
msgid "Conventions to follow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:80
msgid ""
"These are active convention specs whose scope globs match the files being"
" touched. The agent must follow these unless the spec explicitly says "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:82
msgid "If a convention is listed, the agent should:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:83
msgid "Read the convention's full spec if the summary isn't enough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:84
msgid "Follow the pattern described in the convention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:85
msgid ""
"Flag any case where following the convention conflicts with the spec's "
"requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:87
msgid "Past work in this area"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:89
msgid ""
"Completed specs that previously touched the same files. This tells the "
"agent what was done before, why, and what patterns were established. It "
"prevents the agent from undoing previous work or introducing "
"inconsistencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:91
msgid "Use past work to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:92
msgid "Understand the design rationale for existing code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:93
msgid "Identify patterns the agent should continue following"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:94
msgid "Spot potential conflicts between the current spec and prior changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:96
msgid "Decisions that apply"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"Accepted architectural decision records (ADRs). These are constraints the"
" agent must respect. An accepted decision means the team deliberately "
"chose this path — the agent should not revisit the decision unless the "
"spec explicitly says to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:100
msgid "Known risks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:102
msgid ""
"Bug specs whose root causes involved the same files. These are landmines "
"— the agent needs to know about them to avoid triggering the same "
"failures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:104
msgid "Use known risks to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:105
msgid "Add defensive checks in areas with past bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:106
msgid "Avoid patterns that previously caused failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:107
msgid "Include regression tests for known failure modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:109
msgid "Incorporating context into engineer instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:111
msgid "When delegating to an engineer agent, structure the handoff as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:113
msgid "The spec (what to build)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:114
msgid "The context block (what to be aware of)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:115
msgid "Any delivery lead commentary (overrides, priorities, sequencing)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:117
msgid ""
"The context block goes between the spec and any additional instructions. "
"This lets the agent read the spec first, then calibrate its approach "
"based on context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:119
msgid ""
"Do not strip sections from the context block to save tokens. The block is"
" already summarized — removing sections creates blind spots. If a section"
" is genuinely irrelevant, you can add a note saying \"the X section is "
"not relevant to this task because Y\" rather than removing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:121
msgid "When to override or ignore context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:123
msgid "Context is guidance, not law. Override it when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:125
msgid ""
"**The spec intentionally changes a convention.** If the work is to "
"migrate from one pattern to another, the old convention should not "
"constrain the new work. Add a note: \"Convention X is being superseded by"
" this work — do not follow it for new code.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:126
msgid ""
"**A past decision is being revisited.** If the spec explicitly "
"reconsiders an accepted decision, note this and explain why the decision "
"no longer applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:127
msgid ""
"**Past work context is stale.** If the referenced past spec is old enough"
" that the code has changed significantly since, note this so the agent "
"verifies current state rather than relying on the summary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:129
msgid ""
"Never silently ignore context. If you're overriding something, say so and"
" explain why. This creates a trail that future context lookups can "
"surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:131
msgid "Handling conflicting context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:133
msgid "When context sections contradict each other or the spec:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:135
msgid ""
"**Convention vs. spec requirement**: The spec wins. Add a note that the "
"convention needs updating after this work lands, or that this is an "
"intentional exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:136
msgid ""
"**Past decision vs. new requirement**: Escalate. If the spec didn't "
"explicitly address the conflict, pause delivery and raise the conflict to"
" the spec author. The decision may need to be superseded with a new "
"decision spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"**Two conventions conflict**: This is a convention-authoring bug. Flag "
"it. One convention should be updated to exclude the overlapping scope, or"
" the two should be consolidated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:138
msgid ""
"**Past work vs. known risk**: Both inform the agent. Past work shows what"
" was done; known risks show what went wrong. They don't conflict — the "
"agent should use both to inform its approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:140
msgid "Quality check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:142
msgid "Before handing off to the engineer, verify:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:143
msgid ""
"The context block was generated from the correct file paths (not stale or"
" wrong paths)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:144
msgid "No convention listed has been superseded since the last index rebuild"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:145
msgid "Any overrides are explicitly noted with rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/context-injection/SKILL.md:146
msgid ""
"The combined spec + context is not so large that it will exceed the "
"agent's effective context window"
msgstr ""

